        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 2 2\n1 5\n2 10\n1 2 6\n2 3 9\n3 2 2\n1 5\n2 10\n1 2 1\n2 3 9",
        "output": "5 10 19 \n5 6 15",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The hospitals are situated at cities 111 and 222 with their costs being 555 and 10 respectively. For city 111 it is optimal to test the sample in its own hospital bearing a total cost of 555. For city 222 it is again optimal to test the sample in its own hospital bearing a total cost of 101010. For city 333 it is optimal to test the sample in the hospital at city 222 which incurs the traveling cost of 999 and hospital cost of 101010, so the total cost is 10+9=1910+9=1910+9=19.\nTest case 222: For city 222, it is optimal to test the sample in hospital at city 111 which incurs a traveling cost of 111 and hospital cost of 555, so the total cost is 1+5=61+5=61+5=6."
